# Patrol: drive the configured search route until a target is confirmed, approach it,
# and hold it centred and large on screen at the standoff distance.
#
# target_class narrows the mission to ONE class (e.g. "person"). Empty = any of the
# node's configured `target_classes`. A non-empty class outside that list is rejected
# at goal time: the tracker will never publish it, so the mission could only fail slowly.
string target_class
---
# true only when the target was confirmed AND held on screen at the standoff pose.
bool found
# The confirmed target in the map frame (identity orientation: the tracker claims a
# position, not a heading). Meaningful only when found is true.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped target_pose
# Human-readable outcome, mirrored in the node's log.
string message
---
# Current mission state: PROBE, SEARCHING, APPROACHING or HOLDING.
string state
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped robot_pose
# Seconds since the goal was accepted (sim time when use_sim_time is set).
float32 elapsed_s
